n, his arm wrapped around the waist of a particularly enthusiastic girl.\n\n \"Maxwell, really?\" Jordan muttered under his breath, shaking his head. He had tried to get Maxwell to stay and help clean up, but Maxwell was determined. \"Come on, it's just one more drink,\" Maxwell had said, winking. Now, the two frat brothers were living in a house that was rapidly becoming a warzone.\n\n---\n\n**Chapter 2: Cops Arrive**\n\nThe sound of squelching tires and blaring sirens cut through the noise. Jordan's heart sank. He knew this was coming. The neighbors had been complaining for hours, their shouts growing louder until they couldn't be ignored. The door burst open, and two cops, looking tired but determined, strode in.\n\n \"Okay, calm down,\" Jordan said, holding up his hands in a peace gesture. His voice was calm but strained. \"This is just... a little too much.\"\n\n \"What's going on here?\" one cop asked, his tone sharp. He was a burly guy with a thick mustache, his eyes scanning the room.\n\n \"Just a party,\" Jordan said, trying to keep his cool. \"It... got a bit out of hand.\"\n\n \"Bit?\" the other cop said, raising an eyebrow. She was tall and no-nonsense, her hair a sleek ponytail. \"I've seen worse. Who's in charge here?\"\n\n \"Uh, I don't know,\" Jordan said, glancing over at Maxwell. Maxwell was still grinning, his arm around the girl's waist. He noticed the cops and gave them a wave, as if he'd just seen an old friend.\n\n \"Oh, great,\" Jordan muttered. He could just imagine what the cops thought.\n\n---\n\n**Chapter 3: Interactions with Cops**\n\nThe cops approached Maxwell and the group around him. Maxwell, ever the charmer, stepped forward, his smile widening. \"Hey, officers!\" he said, extending his hand. \"How can I help you today?\"\n\n \"We're here to talk to you,\" the first cop said, grabbing Maxwell's arm. Maxwell winced but didn't pull away. \"You got complaints from the neighbors about... well, I don't know what, but it sounds serious.\"