ian students might approach science with a focus on moral and ethical implications rather than practical applications. While this isn't to say they're less interested in science, it can influence their mindset towards the subject, potentially leading to a different approach to learning.\n\nThe role of the teacher cannot be underestimated. If the teacher uses methods that resonate with Sikh students, such as incorporating examples or activities that"}
