es and the requirement to fast during Ramadan. Hinduism, however, is more flexible, with various paths or denominations (like Vaishnavism, Shaivism) that can have different practices and beliefs.\n\nSo, summarizing, the religious practices of Muslims and Hindus differ in their focus on central deities or symbols, the role of sacred texts, community involvement, and the structure and rigidity of their practices. Muslims have a more centralized and codified system around Allah, while Hindus have a diverse range of deities and practices that can vary widely.\n<|im_end|>"}
